What:   builds shpool against gosh-shpool's shpool_vt100 (vt100/ with seam/vt100 applied, built
        at .build/vt100) instead of the one on crates.io, for its line-mode restore fix. Tests:
        lines_restore_ends_with_the_prompt shows the fix on Linux (it fails with shpool_vt100
        as published); lines_restore only passed because of the bug (it ran a command after
        "echo foo", so "foo" was not in the last 2 lines) and now runs just "echo foo";
        dynamic_session_restore_mode, which caught the bug on macOS, is no longer skipped there.
Where:  Cargo.toml ([patch.crates-io]), Cargo.lock (shpool_vt100 from a path), shpool/tests/attach.rs.
Shape:  changes a dependency's source; shpool's own code is unchanged.
Needs:  02-macos-tests.patch before it, and tools/build.sh to have built .build/vt100.
Status: upstream, once shpool_vt100 releases the fix: a version bump in shpool instead of the
        [patch.crates-io], with these tests.

